tz-lookup (timezone boundary dataset)
============================================================================
Copyright © The Dark Sky Company, LLC
https://github.com/darkskyapp/tz-lookup
License: CC0-1.0 — copyright and neighbouring rights waived to the extent
possible by law. npm package: tz-lookup@6.1.25

Used by apps/api to resolve birthplace coordinates to an IANA timezone id
without calling an external geocoding service, which would put a birthplace in
a third party's hands. The encoded boundary raster is derived from Evan
Siroky's timezone-boundary-builder, release 2019b.

Two consequences of that vintage, both handled in
apps/api/src/services/timezone.ts rather than left implicit: boundary changes
made after 2019 are not in the dataset, and the compression is lossy near
borders. Coordinates within roughly 11 km of a boundary are reported at
reduced confidence for that reason.

The tz database itself is not vendored. Zone rules come from the tzdb each
runtime already carries — luxon's in apps/calc-stub, the platform's Intl
elsewhere — and the release a chart was calculated against is recorded on the
snapshot as tzdb_version.

